    post:
      summary: Create Rule
      tags:
      - v3.3/rules
      description: |
        The Triage Rules API supports GET, POST, PUT, and DELETE.

        This path's POST method supports two different creation tasks
        depending on the request body.

        **Task A**

        When specifying a new triage category in the request body
        without a detection list, this endpoint creates new Triage Rules.

        The following format is required for source_conditions
        and additional_conditions in the request body:

        The format for Triage rules is based on AND/OR logic,
        making them more flexible and customizable to your specific situation.
        Both 'source_conditions' and 'additional_conditions' are now
        saved as JSON blobs which represents a tree-like structure.
        Each tree node is represented in the following format:

        ```
        {operator: operand}
        ```

        Where "operator" is any of the following:

        ```
        For non-leaf nodes: 'AND' or 'OR'
        For leaf nodes: 'ANY_OF' or 'NONE_OF'
        ```

        The format for "operand" also depends on the type of node.

        For non-leaf nodes, use a list of children tree nodes of the form:

        ```
        [{operator: operand}, {operator: operand}, ...]
        ```

        For leaf nodes, use a dictionary of the form:

        ```
        {
          'field': <FIELD NAME>,
          'values': [{'value': [<VALUE>]}],
          'group': [{'value': [<GROUP ID>]}]
        }
        ```

        Stipulations on the format of the top-level tree structure
        is that the top-level operator must be an 'OR' node, with
        a single 'AND' node as the only child. The 'AND' node may have an arbitrary number
        of leaf node children. All valid Triage rules will look as follows:

        ```
        {
          'OR': [
            {
              'AND': [
                <LEAF NODE 1>,
                <LEAF NODE 2>,
                ...
                <LEAF NODE N>,
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
        ```

        Note 'source_conditions' and 'additional_conditions' have different fields
        that can be used in their leaf nodes. For 'source_conditions', the following
        fields are valid: ip, host, account, sensor. The fields 'ip' and 'host'
        also support triaging on groups, meaning that an IP or a host leaf node can
        be given an IP Group or Host Group ID, and the Triage rule will apply to
        every IP/host in the specified group. For 'additional_conditions', the following
        fields are valid: remote1_ip, remote1_proto, remote1_port, remote1_dns, remote2_ip,
        remote2_proto, remote2_port, remote2_dns, account, named_pipe, uuid,
        identity, share, extensions, rdp client name, rdp client token, keyboard name.
        The fields 'remote1_ip', 'remote2_ip', 'remote1_dns', 'remote2_dns' support
        triaging on groups. Either 'source_conditions' or 'additional_conditions' may
        be null. Setting source_conditions to null implies that this Triage rule with
        apply to All Hosts.

        **Task B**

        The POST Triage Rules endpoint can be used with a
        request body specifying detection ids and a triage category
        to filter a set of detections under the chosen triage category
      operationId: v3.3_rules_create
      parameters:
      - in: body
        name: data
        required: true
        schema:
          oneOf:
          - title: Task A
            description: The request schema for Task A.
            $ref: '#/definitions/RuleRequestBodyV3'
          - type: object
            title: Task B
            description: The request schema for Task B.
            properties:
              detectionIdList:
                description: Detections ids to add to triage rule filter.
                items:
                  type: integer
                  example: 1
                type: array
              triage_category:
                type: string
                example: Benign Detection
                description: Custom Triage label used to categorize specified detections.
      responses:
        '400':
          description: 'Invalid input error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error400JsonParse'
        '422':
          description: 'Invalid input error.'
          schema:
            oneOf:
              - $ref: '#/definitions/Error422PostRulesInvalidField'
              - $ref: '#/definitions/Error422PostRulesConditionsField'
              - $ref: '#/definitions/Error422PostRulesDetectionList'
        '401':
          description: 'Authentication error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error401'
        '403':
          description: 'Authorization error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error403'
        '413':
          description: 'Response too large error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error413'
        '429':
          description: 'Too many requests error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error429'
        '500':
          description: 'Unexpected error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error500'
        '503':
          description: 'Service unavailable error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error503'
        '504':
          description: 'Time out error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error504'
        '201':
          description: ''
          schema:
            oneOf:
            - type: object
              title: Task A
              description: The response for Task A.
              properties:
                id:
                  type: integer
                  description: Rule ID. 
                  example: 1
                _meta:
                  type: object
                  properties:
                    level:
                      type: string
                      description: Success status of operation. 
                      example: Success
                    message:
                      type: string
                      description: Message of success status of operation. 
                      example: "Successfully created triage filter"
            - type: object
              title: Task B
              description: The response for Task B.
              properties:
                ids:
                  type: array
                  items:
                    type: integer
                    example: 1
                  description: Rule IDs. 
                _meta:
                  type: object
                  properties:
                    level:
                      type: string
                      description: Success status of operation. 
                      example: Success
                    message:
                      type: string
                      description: Message of success status of operation. 
                      example: "Successfully created triage filter"
