  /api/v3.3/threatFeeds/:
    get:
      summary: Get Threatfeed List
      operationId: v3.3_threatFeeds_list
      description: |
        The threat feeds API can be used to automate the upload of
        STIX files for threat intelligence matching. The API endpoint
        can also be used to retrieve the current list of threat feed objects already configured in
        the system.

        This endpoint is used to obtain the list of threat feeds (GET).

        API responses may vary depending on product subscriptions (Network, AWS, M365).
      parameters:
      - name: page
        in: query
        description: A page number within the paginated result set.
        required: false
        type: integer
      - name: page_size
        in: query
        description: Number of results to return per page.
        required: false
        type: integer
      - description: Which field to use when ordering the results.
        in: query
        name: ordering
        required: false
        type: string
        enum: 
        - 'name'
        - 'lastUpdatedBy'
        - 'lastUpdated'
        - 'category'
        - 'certainty'
        - 'expiration'
      - name: name
        type: string
        description: Filter by feed name.
        in: query
      - name: category
        type: string
        in: query
        description: Filter by feed category.
        enum:
        - cnc
        - lateral
        - exfil
      - name: certainty
        type: string
        in: query
        description: Filter by feed certainty.
        enum:
        - High
        - Medium
        - Low
      - name: expiration
        type: string
        in: query
        format: date-time
        description: Filter by feed expiration date.
      - name: last_updated
        type: string
        in: query
        format: date-time
        description: Filter by feed last updated date.
      - name: last_updated_by
        type: string
        in: query
        description: Filter feeds by the user making the last update.
      - name: expiration_gte
        type: string
        in: query
        format: date-time
        description: Filter by feed expiration greater than the given date.
      - name: expiration_lte
        type: string
        in: query
        format: date-time
        description: Filter by feed expiration less than the given date.
      - name: last_updated_gte
        type: string
        in: query
        format: date-time
        description: Filter by feed latest update greater than the given date.
      - name: last_updated_lte
        type: string
        in: query
        format: date-time
        description: Filter by feed latest update less than the given date.
      responses:
        '422':
          description: The ordering param requested is invalid.
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error422GetThreatfeeds'
        '404':
          description: The requested page does not exist. Reduce the requested page.
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error404InvalidPage' 
        '400':
          description: 'Invalid query parameter or parameter value.'
          schema:
            oneOf:
              - $ref: '#/definitions/Error400InvalidParams'
              - $ref: '#/definitions/Error400InvalidParamValue'
        '401':
          description: 'Authentication error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error401'
        '403':
          description: 'Authorization error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error403'
        '413':
          description: 'Response too large error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error413'
        '429':
          description: 'Too many requests error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error429'
        '500':
          description: 'Unexpected error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error500'
        '503':
          description: 'Service unavailable error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error503'
        '504':
          description: 'Time out error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error504'
        '200':
          description: ''
          schema:
            oneOf:
            - type: object
              title: 'Success'
              properties:
                count:
                  type: integer
                  example: 1
                next:
                  format: uri
                  type: string
                  x-nullable: true
                  example: https://VECTRA_PORTAL_URL/api/v3.3/threatFeeds?page=2&page_size=1
                previous:
                  format: uri
                  type: string
                  x-nullable: true
                  example: null
                results:
                  items:
                    $ref: '#/definitions/ThreatFeedSerializerV3_3'
            - $ref: '#/definitions/Response200NtCCheck'
      tags:
      - v3.3/threatFeeds
    post:
      summary: Create Threatfeed
      operationId: v3.3_threatFeeds_create
      description: |
        The threat feeds API can be used to automate the upload of
        STIX files for threat intelligence matching. The API endpoint
        can also be used to retrieve the current list of threat feed objects already configured in
        the system.

        This endpoint is used to create a new threat Feed (POST).

        API responses may vary depending on product subscriptions (Network, AWS, M365).
      parameters:
      - name: data
        in: body
        required: true
        schema:
          type: object
          properties:
            threatFeed:
              type: object
              properties:
                name:
                  type: string
                  example: Example name
                defaults:
                  type: object
                  description: Dictionary describing threat feed default
                    values. 
                  properties:
                    indicatorType:
                      type: string
                      enum:
                      - Anonymization
                      - C2
                      - Exfiltration
                      - Malware Artifacts
                      - Watchlist
                      example: Anonymization
                    certainty:
                      type: string
                      enum:
                      - Low
                      - Medium
                      - High
                      example: High
                    duration:
                      type: integer
                      example: 7
                    category:
                      type: string
                      enum:
                      - cnc
                      - exfil
                      - lateral
                      example: cnc
                  required:
                    - indicatorType
                    - certainty
                    - category
          required:
            - treatFeed
      responses:
        '422':
          description: 'Invalid input error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error422PostThreatfeeds'
        '409':
          description: 'Conflict error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error409PostThreatfeeds'
        '400':
          description: 'JSON syntax error in request body.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error400PostThreatfeeds'
        '401':
          description: 'Authentication error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error401'
        '403':
          description: 'Authorization error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error403'
        '413':
          description: 'Response too large error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error413'
        '429':
          description: 'Too many requests error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error429'
        '500':
          description: 'Unexpected error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error500'
        '503':
          description: 'Service unavailable error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error503'
        '504':
          description: 'Time out error.'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Error504'
        '200':
          description: 'Network to SaaS not available'
          schema:
            $ref: '#/definitions/Response200NtCCheck'
        '201':
          description: ''
          schema:
            type: object
            properties:
              threatFeed:
                type: object
                properties:
                  name:
                    type: string
                    description: The name of the threat feed. 
                    example: Example feed
                  id:
                    type: string
                    description: The ID of the threat feed. 
                    example: 5ra34a3t78c6jk0b65494a84jrkc09c3
                  defaults:
                    type: object
                    description: Dictionary describing threat feed default
                      values. 
                    properties:
                      indicatorType:
                        type: string
                        description: Indicator Type of the threat feed. 
                        example: C2
                      certainty:
                        type: string
                        description: Certainty of the threat feed. 
                        example: High
                      duration:
                        type: integer
                        descrption: Duration of the threat feed until expiration. 
                        example: 90
                      category:
                        type: string
                        description: Threat Feed Category (lateral, cnc, exfil). 
                        example: cnc
